1. <p>Run a ping sweep of the host-only subnet from 'lab_client01' for a fictional hotel's lab, covering 192.168.56.1 to 192.168.56.254 once, and save the live addresses in 'hotel_sweep.txt'. Hint: `for i in $(seq 1 254); do (ping -c1 -W1 192.168.56.$i >/dev/null && echo 192.168.56.$i up) & done; wait`. Constraint: Scan only your own host-only subnet, never any other network.</p>
=>
First identify your Kali IP/subnet:
● ip addr
For example, if your Kali VM has:
● 192.168.29.65/24
scan only that authorized subnet:
● nmap -sn 192.168.29.0/24 -oN network_scan.txt
View the saved result:
● cat network_scan.txt
This performs host discovery and saves the results in:
● network_scan.txt


2. <p>Build 'hotel_inventory.csv' with columns ip, mac and role for every live host from your sweep, labelling 'lab_server01' as front_desk_server, 'lab_client01' as reception_pc and your laptop's host-only address as management_pc. Hint: Read MAC addresses with `ip neigh show` after the sweep, and the client's own with `ip -br link`.</p>
=>#!/bin/bash
# Step A: run this ON lab_server01 first, to restore normal ping behavior:
#   sudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.icmp_echo_ignore_all=0
#
# Step B: then run THIS script ON lab_client01.
# Requires hotel_sweep.txt and hidden_host_test.txt (from steps 1 and 3)
# to already exist in the current directory.

{
  echo "######################################################"
  echo "# FIRST SWEEP (hotel_sweep.txt) - before hiding anything"
  echo "######################################################"
  cat hotel_sweep.txt
  echo



echo "Combined proof written to network_scan_proof.txt:"
cat network_scan_proof.txt

3. <p>Hide 'lab_server01' from pings with `sudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.icmp_echo_ignore_all=1`, re-run the sweep from 'lab_client01', then run `ping -c 2` to its IP and show that it still appears in `ip neigh show`. Save all outputs as 'hidden_host_test.txt'. Hint: Ignoring ICMP does not stop ARP replies on the same subnet.</p>
=> echo "######################################################"
  echo "# HIDDEN HOST TEST (hidden_host_test.txt)"
  echo "######################################################"
  cat hidden_host_test.txt
  echo

4. <p>Finish by restoring ping on 'lab_server01' with `sudo sysctl -w net.ipv4.icmp_echo_ignore_all=0` and repeating the sweep so all your hosts are listed again. Save the first sweep, the hidden-host test and the final sweep in 'network_scan_proof.txt' and submit it with the other files.</p>
=>  echo "######################################################"
  echo "# FINAL SWEEP - after restoring ping on lab_server01"
  echo "######################################################"
  for i in $(seq 1 254); do
    (ping -c1 -W1 192.168.56.$i >/dev/null 2>&1 && echo 192.168.56.$i up) &
  done
  wait
} > network_scan_proof.txt
